Appreciate the engagement from everyone! Quick status: PR #11377 is still open, waiting on maintainer review.

@trevor-vaughan @xintron — you're raising a distinct (and valid) concern about **model resolution UX** (fuzzy matching, sorting, favorites), which is orthogonal to the tier-based selection this PR implements. The tier abstraction solves *"which model does this subagent use"* at the config/schema level. It's the *what*. What you're describing is *how the user/session picks which model goes into that tier* in the UI/CLI.

@xintron the sorting-by-favorites suggestion specifically feels like a UX improvement for the model picker (⌘T or `model:` input), not something the Task tool schema needs to worry about.

I'll keep this issue scoped to the Task tool API (`model_tier` parameter + config resolution). If any of you want to champion the fuzzy matching or model picker sorting, I'd +1 those as follow-ups.
